{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature","title":"def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.md","line":159,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex#def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex","label":"def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature","line":299,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Ricci curvature]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0103}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor}\n\n  For an orthonormal basis $e_1,\\dots,e_n$ of $T_pM$, the \\emph{Ricci curvature} is\n  the trace\n  \\[\n    \\operatorname{Ric}(v,w)=\\operatorname{tr}(x\\mapsto R(x,v)w)\n    =\\sum_{i=1}^ng(R(e_i,v)w,e_i)=\\sum_{i=1}^ng(R(v,e_i)e_i,w)\n    =\\sum_{i=1}^ng(R(e_i,w)v,e_i),\n  \\]\n  a symmetric bilinear form, equivalently the symmetric $(1,1)$-tensor\n  $\\operatorname{Ric}(v)=\\sum_{i=1}^nR(v,e_i)e_i$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Ricci curvature] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368332d72696363692d637572766174757265\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0103</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23def%3Apet-ch3-curvature-tensor\">↗ def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor</a> <p></p>For an orthonormal basis <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$e_1,\\dots ,e_n$\">$e_1,\\dots ,e_n$</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_pM$\">$T_pM$</span>, the <em>Ricci curvature</em> is the trace <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\operatorname {Ric}(v,w)=\\operatorname {tr}(x\\mapsto R(x,v)w) =\\sum _{i=1}^ng(R(e_i,v)w,e_i)=\\sum _{i=1}^ng(R(v,e_i)e_i,w) =\\sum _{i=1}^ng(R(e_i,w)v,e_i),  \\]\">\\[  \\operatorname {Ric}(v,w)=\\operatorname {tr}(x\\mapsto R(x,v)w) =\\sum _{i=1}^ng(R(e_i,v)w,e_i)=\\sum _{i=1}^ng(R(v,e_i)e_i,w) =\\sum _{i=1}^ng(R(e_i,w)v,e_i),  \\]</span> a symmetric bilinear form, equivalently the symmetric <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(1,1)$\">$(1,1)$</span>-tensor <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {Ric}(v)=\\sum _{i=1}^nR(v,e_i)e_i$\">$\\operatorname {Ric}(v)=\\sum _{i=1}^nR(v,e_i)e_i$</span>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-constant-curvature","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-einstein-manifold","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor","title":"def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor","label":"def:pet-ch3-curvature-tensor"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-einstein-manifold","title":"def:pet-ch3-einstein-manifold","label":"def:pet-ch3-einstein-manifold"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation","title":"prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation","label":"prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-scalar-curvature","title":"def:pet-ch3-scalar-curvature","label":"def:pet-ch3-scalar-curvature"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-contracted-bianchi","title":"prop:pet-ch3-contracted-bianchi","label":"prop:pet-ch3-contracted-bianchi"},{"kind":"